title: the Banners
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: banner_timer <= 0 and not rb_explode
card-image: img/reichsbanner.jpg
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; banner_timer += 6; rb_militarization_cost = 2 if rb_militancy > 0.1 else rb_militarization_cost = 1; rb_militarization_cost = 3 if rb_militancy > 0.25
max-visits: 6
#subtitle: Paramilitary organizing in defense of the republic.

= the Banners

The *the Banners* <span style="color: #000000;"><b><i>Schwarz</i></b></span>-<span style="color: #DD0000;"><b><i>Rot</i></b></span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;"><b><i>Gold</i></b></span> is a mass organization for the defense of the Republic against the extremists who threaten it. Some would call it a paramilitary, although currently it is hardly any sort of military. It is officially associated with the pro-democratic parties -the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?], and <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, but by far the largest component is with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>.

[? if commons_marcher < 46 or commons_marcher < commons_royalist or commons_marcher < commons_collectivist : The the Banners is having a more difficult time recruiting, as the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> is no longer the dominant party among the workers. Many of its members have left. ?]

- @militant: Fund more military-style training and equipment for the the Banners.
- @militant_2: Use our existing resources to support more training for the the Banners.
- @same: Keep the the Banners as it is.
- @cut_rb: Cut funding for the the Banners.
- @women_rb
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

#- Orient reichsbanner towards anti-fascism (only available if we have prioritized anti fascism)

@militant
choose-if: resources >= rb_militarization_cost
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources ([+ rb_militarization_cost +] needed).
subtitle: -[+ rb_militarization_cost +] resources
on-arrival: resources -= rb_militarization_cost; rb_investment += 1; rb_strength += 100; rb_militancy += 0.05; left_strength += 2; left_dissent -= 2; reformist_dissent += 5; marcher_militancy += 0.05; commons_marcher += 2*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 2*(1-dissent); unionist_relation -= 3 if strife < 5; ddp_relation -= 3 if strife < 5; lvp_relation -= 3 if strife < 5

Some in our party decry the increasing militarization of the the Banners. They say it is emulating the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right-wing nationalists</span> or the <span style="color: #700000;">communists</span>, and risks alienating our allies in the centrist parties. On the other hand, more left-leaning radicals are being lured to our organizations, away from the <span style="color: #700000;">communists</span>.

[? if not concord_leave_banner and not rb_exit: [? if strife < 5: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] decries the militarization of the the Banners, and its members are leaving the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> organization. ?][? if strife >= 5: Seeing the strife that has filled the Commonwealth's streets, the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and [? if not lvp_formed:<span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed:<span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?] seem to be convinced that it is necessary for the the Banners to be militarized, and mute their criticisms. ?] ?]


@militant_2
view-if: funded_banner >= 1
on-arrival: rb_militancy += 0.02; funded_banner -= 1

As we have already funded resources towards the the Banners, we can invest in building up their militancy. 


@same

The the Banners is already serving the purpose it needs to serve. There is no reason to change what already works.

- @return: Continue...


@cut_rb
subtitle: +1 resources
on-arrival: resources += 1; rb_strength -= 100; rb_militancy -= 0.05; left_strength -= 2; left_dissent -= 2; marcher_militancy -= 0.05; commons_collectivist += 2; disfavored_collectivist += 2

Cutting resources to the the Banners causes a drop in the membership, and leads some would-be members to join the <span style="color: #700000;">Communists</span> instead.


@women_rb
title: Allow women to join the the Banners.
subtitle: -1 resources - This might cause a backlash from existing members.
choose-if: resources > 0
view-if: womens_rights >= 4 and sender_advisor == 1 and iron_front_formed == 1
on-arrival: resources -= 1; rb_militancy *= 0.85; rb_strength += 400; women_in_rb = 1; rb_militancy += 0.05 if repealed_175; rb_militancy += 0.04 if trans_rights; rb_militancy += 0.02 if reformed_183;
go-to: homosexual if trans_rights or repealed_175 or reformed_183
max-visits: 1
achievement: women_reichsbanner

The suggestion to allow women into the the Banners is ridiculed by most, except for Toni Sennet. But this is an exceptional time, and we need anyone who is willing to join. Thus, we organize specialized units for women, [? if homosexual_rights > 0: and even some covert units for <span style="color: deepskyblue;">tran</span><span style="color: linen;">sse</span><span style="color: lightpink;">xuals</span> and <span style="color: red;">ho</span><span style="color: orange;">m</span><span style="color: yellow;">os</span><span style="color: green;">ex</span><span style="color: blue;">ua</span><span style="color: purple;">ls</span>?].

After allowing women to join, the number of comrades who leave is more than balanced out by the number of radicalized women and others who join. However, many of our departed members were veterans, and many of the new members have no experience with military-style training.

@homosexual
achievement: anders_als_die_andern